  <h1 class="page-title">Sweepstakes Casino Taxes and Prize Records</h1>
  <p class="lede">Keep complete records of prizes, redemptions and account activity. Tax treatment depends on your facts and jurisdiction, so use these records with a qualified tax professional.</p>
  <div class="answer-first"><span class="af-label">Practical takeaway</span><p>Do not wait for tax season to reconstruct account history. Export statements when available and log each redemption with its request date, received date, value, method and supporting document.</p></div>
  <h2>Records to keep</h2>
  <ul class="tick-list">
    <li class="good"><b>Redemption log.</b> Operator, amount, request date, approval date, received date and method.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Account statements.</b> Save downloadable transaction and play histories before an account closes or a retention window expires.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Payment evidence.</b> Keep bank, gift-card or wallet records that match each redemption.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Operator forms.</b> Retain any tax forms or year-end summaries and note discrepancies promptly.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Supporting costs.</b> Keep records separately and ask a tax professional which items, if any, apply to your situation.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>A simple ledger format</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table class="data"><thead><tr><th>Date requested</th><th>Operator</th><th>Amount</th><th>Method</th><th>Date received</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>YYYY-MM-DD</td><td>Operator name</td><td>Prize value</td><td>Bank, gift card or crypto</td><td>YYYY-MM-DD</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  <p>This page provides general record-keeping information, not tax advice. A CPA or other qualified adviser can apply current federal and state rules to your circumstances.</p>
